other_error_test.error_test:
Any 2 of the following 4 zones exceed their associated threshold:
THRM_REM_1_E1_VLV_ZN_CTRL_TEMP <= REM_1_E1_VLV_THRSH;
THRM_REM_1_E3_VLV_ZN_CTRL_TEMP <= REM_1_E3_VLV_THRSH;
THRM_REM_2_E3_VLV_ZN_CTRL_TEMP <= REM_2_E3_VLV_THRSH;
THRM_REM_2_E2_VLV_ZN_CTRL_TEMP <= REM_2_E2_VLV_THRSH

Detector HV field (HVPSDETVOLT) in the SUDA H&S packet reports a voltage reading greater than or equal to a parametrized threshold value (i.e. HVPSDETVOLT >= 100 Volts, where 100 Volts is the threshold limit);

AND

TRUE == acs_ctl_get_is_suda_const_in_viol();

Error Test Notes: 
The HVPSDETVOLT field spans bits /198:4-/199:7 in the SUDA H&S packet. This field is channelized into ground derived channel SUDA-4120 SUDA_HVPS_DET_VOLTAGE by the SUDA Instrument Manager. This field is also channelized into SC FSW channel SUDA-0044 SUDA_HVPS_STATUS_1, and occupies the first 12 bits of that channel.

acs_ctl_get_is_suda_const_in_viol() is a public get function provided by the GNC FSW to note if the Sun is in the SUDA KOZ. TRUE == acs_ctl_get_is_suda_const_in_viol() means the Sun is in the KOZ.

monitor.monitor_description:
Detects if the DSS data is invalid for unacceptably long period of time. To determine incorrect DSS data, the SDE performs the following checks at 8 Hz: 
1) DSS data invalid;
2) Timetag difference >= TIMETAG_TOO_OLD_THRSH;
3) Invalid Gray code combination

